## SQ-RPS-01 | isolated boot: ladder loads clean, nested mods found
@group B
@commands Boot with `rps only`. `grep -nE "Diet ladder|Raspberry Pie|solapplepie|solcarrot|Mixin apply|Missing or unsupported" logs/latest.log` (RPS-01)
@pass exactly one `Diet ladder:` info line naming 4 slots; no `Diet ladder (` warning line; no missing-dependency, mixin or injection error; `Done (` reached
@fails nested jar metadata or version range in `mods.toml` / `ce.forge-bundle.gradle` (P1); default ladder file (P2); a mixin target that needs a mod the standalone set lacks (P4, P6)
@from plan_rp_standalone.md section 6
bootexpect Diet ladder: \d+ rungs, 4 slots
bootreject Diet ladder \(
bootreject Missing or unsupported mandatory|InvalidInjectionException|Mixin apply.*solraspberrypie.*failed|MixinApplyError|Encountered an unexpected exception
look the `Diet ladder:` line appears once in the whole log (grep -c); the rung count is the default ladder's 17 attribute rungs plus 10 unlocks, as P2 wrote them
## CQ-RPS-02 | isolated client: names, Apple Pie book and potato recipe gone, book recipes work
@group client
@commands Client with `rps only`, new survival world. Inventory, `/recipe`-free: open the crafting table and JEI-free recipe book; craft book + bread, book + apple juice or any drink, book + carrot (RPS-02)
@pass the book is named Diet Log, the second book Food Dictionary (not Apple Pie's names); Apple Pie's own book recipe and its potato recipe are absent; book + food gives a Diet Log, book + drink a Liquid Diet Log
@fails Raspberry Pie `assets/solraspberrypie/lang/en_us.json` and `client/LangOverrides.java` (names, P4); `RecipeManagerMixin` (recipe removal must run without KubeJS)
@draft client steps: crafting-table slots, names read by the capture driver
## CQ-RPS-03 | isolated client: no diversity table, Apple Pie food values stand, tooltips and books agree
@group client
@commands Client with `rps only`, no diversity file on the classpath. Eat or inspect bread, apple, golden apple, cake; open the Diet Log (RPS-03)
@pass no table loaded (one INFO line, no warning); each food's tooltip diversity value equals Apple Pie's own value for it; the Diet Log shows the same value after eating
@fails `Diversity` loader (P3): no-file case must not override; the tooltip mixin reading a different source than the book
@draft client steps and the reference values (read Apple Pie's own tooltip values from the nested jar)
## SQ-RPS-04 | loose Apple Pie 2.2.0 beside the nested copy: one loads, no crash
@group B
@modset rps loose
@commands Boot with `rps loose` (loose `solapplepie-1.19.2-2.2.0.jar` in `mods/` next to the nested one) (RPS-04)
@pass server reaches `Done (`; no duplicate-mod crash and no `ModFileDuplicate`/`Duplicate` error; the log names one `solapplepie` mod file; one `Diet ladder:` line
@fails Jar-in-Jar version range in `ce.forge-bundle.gradle` (P1); Forge picks the higher or loose version: both are 2.2.0, so the nested jar must be skipped without an error
bootexpect Done \(
bootexpect Diet ladder: \d+ rungs, 4 slots
bootreject Duplicate|duplicate mod|ModFileDuplicate|DuplicateModsFoundException|Encountered an unexpected exception
look `grep -n "solapplepie" logs/latest.log` shows one loaded mod file for solapplepie
## CQ-RPS-05 | Apple Pie defaults: eat, respec, drop, die; ageing-out and gate
@group client
@commands Client with `rps only` (Apple Pie settings at their defaults: `queueSize` 32, `minFoodsToActivate` 0). Eat a run of different foods past 32 entries, respec at the ladder screen, drop a food, die (RPS-05)
@pass eating adds diversity and the 33rd distinct food ages the oldest out at the cost plan 6.1 gives; the unique-food gate refuses a repeat; respec refunds and re-applies the ladder; dropping and dying leave state consistent (`resetOnDeath` default); start log has no Raspberry Pie warning (`minContribution` is 0)
@fails ageing-out cost and gate in `raspberry_pie.md` 6.1 and the gate code (P5); the warning list in the config check (P5)
@draft client steps: eat loop with `/give`, respec command, `/kill`
## SQ-RPS-06 | Alex's Mobs present: Fleet-Footed mixin applies
@group B
@modset rps alex
@commands Boot with `rps alex` (Alex's Mobs 1.19.2 and Citadel beside the Raspberry Pie jar) (RPS-06)
@pass `Done (` reached; the Fleet-Footed mixin applies (no skip warning from Raspberry Pie); no mixin error
@fails `FleetFootedMixin` and the member check in its mixin plugin (P6); Alex's Mobs version differs from the ranged one in the writeup
bootexpect Done \(
bootreject Fleet-Footed.*skipp|FleetFooted.*skipp|InvalidInjectionException|Mixin apply.*solraspberrypie.*failed|MixinApplyError
look no warning about EffectFleetFooted anywhere in latest.log; the mixin is listed as applied if `-Dmixin.debug` output is present
## SQ-RPS-08 | Alex's Mobs stub missing a field: mixin skipped, one warning, no crash
@group B
@modset rps alex
@commands Boot with `rps alex` after a stub swap: the Alex's Mobs jar is replaced by a copy whose `EffectFleetFooted` lacks a field the mixin touches (second half of RPS-06; id 08 because the plan's single RPS-06 needs two boots)
@pass `Done (` reached; exactly one Raspberry Pie warning naming the skipped Fleet-Footed mixin; no crash, no mixin error
@fails the member check and `require = 0` in `FleetFootedMixin` / its plugin (P6)
@draft fixture: a tools/ script that builds the stub jar from the pack's Alex's Mobs jar (rewrites `EffectFleetFooted` without one field); the first runner writes it, then `edit` swaps the jar before `restart`
## SQ-RPS-07 | in the pack: table split, unknown id loads, count logged once
@group B
@modset none
@commands Pack server (full pack, Creative Delight carries the pack table). Add a scratch diversity table file with an unknown food id on the classpath, boot (RPS-07)
@pass the server boots; one INFO line gives the count of skipped unknown ids (no per-id warning); other ids in the same file apply (`/cdevtest` reads or the tooltip value of a known id in the file matches it)
@fails `Diversity` loader merge and optional-id handling (P3); the table's new location in Creative Delight (P8)
